  "scope": "Charm and sound across the installer phases on controller and native FreeBSD pseudo-terminals, and the OSS write path on a FreeBSD 16 host's real HDMI pcm device. No 1.4 image was built, no installation was run and nothing was heard on an exact image.",
  "operator_direction": [
    "A lot of pizazz: Daemonarchy 1.4 must be much more charming and interesting to watch through all phases of installation.",
    "Use sounds liberally; animations should make noise.",
    "Stay truthful: animation never fakes progress.",
    "Procedural sounds only; OSS playback that never blocks; mute/volume keys, a configurator option and a loader default; automatic silence on serial/headless, unattended and no-device.",
    "The loader gets visual charm only, in daemonarchy-src."
