  "findings": [
    "The first native run failed the tmux completion case: the sound indicator truncated the 'Close the other panes' footer in a split pane. Important footer messages now keep the whole row and narrow footers use the short indicator.",
    "On the controller and FreeBSD hosts tests/installer-clock.sh (BSD date), tests/live-backend.sh (GNU stat) and tests/live-desktop.sh (python3 name) are platform-specific and fail identically on origin/main where they cannot run.",
    "A file-backed device keeps its recording aligned with the wall clock, so each demo's .ogg plays in step with its cast.",
    "An earlier native run of tests/vt-console-colors.py started the sound player on the host's real default device (pcm1), so a few cues played aloud on the test host, and FreeBSD timeout(1), a process reaper, then waited for that player. The test now sets DAEMONARCHY_SOUND=off and a private sound directory, installer-progress tests use a nonexistent device unless they pass a file, and the player now exits after 15 minutes without hearing from a front end (the install screen checks in every 30 seconds; `sound play` restarts it).",
    "A tmux test's cleanup looked up the sound directory before the session existed and left a player running; it now passes a known directory."
  ],
